schema: "0.4"
id: chalkboard-11-setup-wizard
type: image
quality: high

# The Robot Learns — a terminal study CLI. Setup Wizard — the guided first-run flow (install,
# detect machine, build profile, seed KB, tour commands), rendered as a chalkboard terminal.
# Theme tenets: always-dark forest-green slate board, warm chalk-white hand-lettering, dusty
# colored-chalk accents used categorically (never neon), flat radius-0 board, dashed chalk
# rules + hand-drawn underline/step-line for emphasis (never bold weight); warning reinforced
# with an underline/icon since rose chalk is both a brand and the error hue.
# Palette: board green #2d4a2d, near-black board #1e2a1e, chalk-white #e8e4d8, sand-chalk
# #c8c0a8, yellow chalk #e8d44c, blue chalk #6cb4dc, rose chalk #e06060, sage chalk #50b878.

prompt:
  system: |
    You are a senior product designer rendering a high-fidelity UI mockup of a warm,
    always-dark TERMINAL session skinned as a professor's chalkboard — a single focused
    terminal window, not a web page and not a browser. The surface is a guided first-run setup
    wizard drawn out on the board like a lesson plan: a numbered step line across the top and
    the current step filling the board. Questions and labels are hand-lettered in a casual
    print-handwriting face; detected OS/tool values and keys stay in a neat monospace. Emphasis
    is an underline or a drawn tick, never a bold weight. Colored chalk is dusty and desaturated,
    never neon. Flat board, square corners, dashed chalk rules, a faint dust of chalk texture.
  text: |
    A 16:9 high-fidelity mockup of a focused single-pane TERMINAL session — "The Robot
    Learns" — skinned as a dark green chalkboard, running the first-run setup wizard. One warm
    forest-green slate board fills the frame like a terminal window. NO browser chrome, NO tabs,
    NO address bar, NO web page.

    OVERALL LAYOUT: a numbered step line across the top and the current step filling the board
    below it.

    TOP is a SETUP STEP INDICATOR — a row of five numbered chalk circles connected by a
    hand-drawn chalk line, labeled "1 install · 2 detect · 3 profile · 4 seed · 5 tour"; step 3
    is circled in bright chalk and underlined to show it is current, the first two ticked with
    small sage-chalk checkmarks.

    The dominant CENTER is the current step, a PROFILE SELECTOR. A written question in display
    handwriting reads "How well do you know each area?"; below it a short list of domains each
    with a three-notch chalk scale labeled "beginner · intermediate · expert", the chosen notch
    marked with a chalk tick — "Algorithms" set to intermediate, "Elixir" set to expert,
    "French" set to beginner.

    Beside it a MACHINE / ENVIRONMENT PROFILE card, a dashed chalk-outlined region under the
    label "we detected", lists auto-found values in monospace with small sage-chalk checkmarks,
    "macOS 14 · zsh · node 20 · git 2.44".

    An ERROR / WARNING BANNER sits as a hand-drawn chalk-outlined strip in dusty rose chalk with
    an underline and a small warning doodle, reading "Claude Code not found on PATH — install it
    to continue", the rose reinforced by the icon so it does not read as ordinary red chalk.

    A CONFIRMATION PROMPT at the bottom is a written line "Ready to seed a few starter topics?"
    with two chalk-outlined choices "[ y ] keep going" and "[ n ] cancel", the yes underlined. A
    faint monospace status line reads "safe to re-run · nothing overwritten".

    PALETTE & TYPE: a deep forest-green slate board as the canvas, one slightly lighter green
    panel for the detected-machine card; lettering in warm dusty chalk-white, secondary labels
    in dimmer sand-chalk. Steps and marks in sticks of dusty colored chalk — a warm butter-yellow
    for the current step, a sage green for ticks, a soft rose-red for the warning — all
    desaturated like real chalk, never bright or neon. Questions and labels hand-lettered in a
    casual print handwriting face; detected values and keys in a neat monospace.

    SHAPE & SURFACE: flat board with square corners, no rounded cards and no glossy panels;
    regions divided by dashed chalk rules; the step circles and the warning strip are hand-drawn
    chalk outlines with slightly uneven edges; a faint even dust of chalk grain and one soft
    eraser smudge.

    MOOD: warm, academic, personal — a patient teacher walking you to your desk on the first
    day, unhurried and reassuring.
  negative: "watermark, signature, lorem ipsum placeholder text, low-fidelity wireframe, monitor/device photograph framing, blurry, distorted UI, browser chrome, address bar, browser tabs, web page, rounded cards, glossy panels, neon or saturated colors, dry-erase whiteboard, pure white or light background, bold heavy type"

output:
  formats:
    - format: png
  dimensions:
    width: 1920
    height: 1080
    aspect_ratio: "16:9"

eval:
  pass_threshold: 0.72
  criteria:
    relevance: {weight: 3, description: "Matches Setup Wizard: a numbered setup step indicator, a profile selector with per-domain expertise scales, a detected machine/environment card, a warning banner, and a confirmation prompt — inside one terminal board"}
    theme_fidelity: {weight: 3, description: "Always-dark forest-green board, warm chalk-white handwriting questions + mono detected values, dusty categorical colored-chalk accents (yellow current step, sage ticks, rose warning; no neon), hand-drawn step line/underline, flat square corners, dashed chalk rules — not generic UI defaults"}
    composition: {weight: 2, description: "Clear top step line over a dominant current-step body, plausible real-product terminal wizard layout"}
    technical: {weight: 2, description: "Sharp, correct 16:9 aspect, no artifacts"}
  reject_if:
    - "lorem ipsum or placeholder text visible"
    - "watermark or signature visible"
    - "wireframe-level fidelity instead of high-fidelity mockup"
    - "browser chrome, tabs, or address bar instead of a terminal window"
    - "neon or saturated colors, or a light/whiteboard background"

tags: [chalkboard, therobotlearns.com, screen-mockup, terminal]
